---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — CloudPriceFinder"
  description="Learn more about CloudPriceFinder — the free, open-source multi-cloud instance cost comparison tool for AWS, Azure, GCP, and OCI."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        About CloudPriceFinder
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        Free, open-source multi-cloud instance cost comparison
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto">
      <h2>What is CloudPriceFinder?</h2>
      <p>
        CloudPriceFinder is a free, open-source tool that helps developers and businesses compare
        cloud compute instance costs across the four major providers: AWS, Azure, Google Cloud (GCP),
        and Oracle Cloud (OCI). Instead of manually checking each cloud provider's pricing pages,
        CloudPriceFinder aggregates and normalizes pricing data — including on-demand and 1-year/3-year
        reserved/committed pricing — so you can make informed decisions quickly.
      </p>
      <p>
        There are no ads, no upselling, and no tracking. Data is refreshed weekly via GitHub Actions
        and served as a static site on Cloudflare Pages.
      </p>

      <h2>Supported Providers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</strong> — EC2 instances with on-demand and Reserved Instance pricing</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Azure</strong> — Virtual Machines with Consumption and Reservation pricing</li>
        <li><strong>Google Cloud Platform (GCP)</strong> — Compute Engine instances with on-demand and Committed Use Discounts (CUDs)</li>
        <li><strong>Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)</strong> — Compute shapes with on-demand pricing (commitment pricing is managed via Universal Credits at account level)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Features</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Real pricing data fetched weekly from public provider APIs — no guesswork, no hardcoded values</li>
        <li>On-demand, 1-year, and 3-year commitment pricing in one view</li>
        <li>Normalized metrics: $/vCPU/hr and $/GiB-RAM/hr for fair comparison</li>
        <li>Side-by-side comparison of up to 4 instances across providers</li>
        <li>Filter by vCPU, memory, provider, architecture, and GPU availability</li>
        <li>Lazy-loaded data — fast initial page load (&lt; 200 KB)</li>
        <li>No tracking, no analytics, no cookies</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Data Sources</h2>
      <p>
        All pricing data is fetched directly from official public provider APIs and pricing endpoints:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>AWS:</strong>{' '}
          <a href="https://pricing.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/offers/v1.0/aws/index.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            AWS Pricing API (offers/v1.0)
          </a>{' '}and{' '}
          <a href="https://pricing.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/offers/v1.0/aws/savingsPlan/v1.0/index.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Savings Plans API
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Azure:</strong>{' '}
          <a href="https://prices.azure.com/api/retail/prices" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Azure Retail Prices API
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GCP:</strong>{' '}
          <a href="https://cloud.google.com/billing/v1/how-tos/catalog-api" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Cloud Billing Catalog API
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OCI:</strong>{' '}
          <a href="https://apexapps.oracle.com/pls/apex/cetools/api/v1/products/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Oracle Cloud Pricing API (cetools)
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
        Prices are converted to USD for comparison. Original currencies are preserved in the raw data.
        Data is refreshed weekly and may lag real-time provider changes. Always verify with the
        provider before purchasing.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-lg p-4 not-prose">
        <p class="text-sm text-yellow-800">
          <strong>Pricing accuracy:</strong> Pricing is fetched weekly from public provider APIs and may not
          reflect the latest changes. Some instance types or regions may be missing. Always verify pricing
          directly with your cloud provider before making purchasing decisions.
          CloudPriceFinder is not affiliated with AWS, Azure, GCP, or OCI.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Open Source</h2>
      <p>
        CloudPriceFinder is completely open source. The data collection scripts, aggregation pipeline,
        and frontend are all available on GitHub under the MIT license.
      </p>

      <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-6 mt-8 not-prose">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-blue-900 mb-2">Contribute or fork</h3>
        <p class="text-blue-800 mb-4">
          Help us improve the tool, add more providers, or run your own instance.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/eSKylezZ/cloudpricefinder.com"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-md hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          View on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2>Creator</h2>
      <p>
        Built and maintained by{' '}
        <a href="https://kyleblenkinsop.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kyle Blenkinsop</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
